Sec. 14. As used in this chapter, "fungus" means any nonchlorophyll-bearing plant of a lower order than mosses and liverworts, including:
(1) rust;
(2) smut;
(3) mildew;
(4) mold;
(5) yeast; and
(6) bacteria;
except those on or in living humans or other animals, and those on or in processed food, beverages, or pharmaceuticals.
[Pre-2008 Recodification Citation: 15-3-3.6-2(14).]
As added by P.L.2-2008, SEC.7.

Sec. 25. As used in this chapter, "pesticide" means:
(1) any substance or mixture of substances intended for:
(A) preventing;
(B) destroying;
(C) repelling; or
(D) mitigating;
a pest; or
(2) any substance or mixture of substances intended for use as a:
(A) plant regulator;
(B) defoliant; or
(C) desiccant.
[Pre-2008 Recodification Citation: 15-3-3.6-2(23).]
As added by P.L.2-2008, SEC.7.
